# Everything here is excluded from the build context -- the tarball the CLI
# uploads to the Docker daemon before a build starts. Without this file that
# upload is roughly 300 MB across 19,000 files, almost all of it dependency
# trees the image rebuilds from lockfiles anyway.

# 108 MB. Reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json, and a host
# node_modules can carry native binaries built for Windows.
node_modules

# 192 MB, and actively harmful: it contains Windows binaries
# (Scripts/python.exe, .pyd files) that mean nothing to a Linux container.
# The image builds its own environment from requirements.txt.
server/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Built by the image, never copied into it. Shipping a host build would
# silently override the one the Dockerfile just made.
dist

# NEVER let a key into the build context. Anything copied into a layer is
# in the image permanently -- deleting it in a later layer does not remove
# it, it just hides it from the final filesystem. .env.example carries the
# shape without the secret and is allowed through.
#
# The ** matters, and its absence was a real bug: these patterns are
# matched against paths relative to the CONTEXT ROOT, so a bare `.env`
# matches only /.env. The file that actually holds the key is
# server/.env, which sailed straight past it and into the image. Verified
# now by grepping the running container rather than by reading this file
# and believing it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Not needed at runtime. The production image ships no test runner, which is
# also why requirements-dev.txt stays out.
**/*.test.js
**/*.test.jsx
server/tests
server/requirements-dev.txt

# Development-only tooling and history.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
README.md
.oxlintrc.json

# The cache is deliberately included -- it is what makes the container work
# with no API key and no network. But only the default subject's files, so
# the image is identical no matter whose machine built it. Any other cached
# player is a local artefact, not part of the project.
server/cache/*
!server/cache/shots-1628983-2025-26.json
!server/cache/splits-1628983-2025-26.json
!server/cache/summary-1628983-2025-26.json
